	(text_box "A T0-92 through hole footprint and a SOT-23-5 SMT footprint are provided in parallel, generally use only U2, U3, or U1.  U1 has a builtin 5V to 3.3V regulator, 3V3OUT.\n\"5V\" can come from USB via the iTrip conenctor, or 3.6V (2xAA), 4.2V, or 6V+ batteries, etc. as long as the regulators are right sized. \n\n3.6V and lower battery packs can be wired directly to the 3.3V connectors, and no regulator is needed.\nThere's no power mixing on the 3.3V line, so it's not generally safe to charge batteries on 3.3V from the regulators, though expert usage allows both the regulator hardware to coexist with 3.3V batteries.   The FTDI 3.3V regulator output is a bit too low to reliably charge batteries."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 96.52 0)
		(size 119.38 71.12)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 194 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b724e5c-2e22-46ff-8f0e-a049aa359ab8")
	)
	(text_box "The FTDI232RL is not the cheapest chip, but it doesn't require any external crystal, EEPROM, or power conversion.  \n\nThe USB connector on the iTrip is routed to the USB to serial converter, and the UART outputs are run back to the LPC936 8051 microcontroller inside the iTrip.  A single FTDI chip can power and communicate with up to 8 iTrips, but only after configuring higher TX pin drive strength via the FT_PROG software.  \nEach iTrip must be configured during firmware programming to a unique MIDI channel, which also limits the number of connections to 8 (16 channels per MIDI bus, and each iTrip responds to 2 channels). \nWire the TX of other iTrips to TX of this board, RX to RX.\n\nSee detailed instructions in the github readme."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 256.54 0)
		(size 119.38 78.74)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 194 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
			(href "https://github.com/exitrip/1010---midi")
		)
		(uuid "1e26b2ec-4598-447d-a0e3-442b93fb986f")
	)
	(text_box "1  Ground (-) 1\n2  Line Out - Common Ground (-) 1\n3  Line Out - R (+)\n4  Line Out - L (+)\n5  Line In - R (+)\n6  Line In - L (+)\n7\n8  Video Out - Composite Video (for ipod colour when slideshow activated) 6\n9  S-Video Chrominance 7\n10 S-Video Luminance 7\n11 Serial GND\n12 Serial TxD\n13 Serial RxD\n14\n15 Ground (-) 2\n16 USB GND (-) 2\n17\n18 3.3V Power (+) 8\n19 Firewire Power 12 VDC (+) 3\n20 Firewire Power 12 VDC (+) 3\n21 Accessory Indicator 4\n22 FireWire Data TPA (-)\n23 USB Power 5 VDC (+) 9\n24 FireWire Data TPA (+)\n25 USB Data (-) 9\n26 FireWire Data TPB (-)\n27 USB Data (+) 9\n28 FireWire Data TPB (+)\n29 FireWire Ground (-) 5\n30 FireWire Ground (-) 5"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
